From: Orion <orionopenwow@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] openvanilla: Duels, straight into the world (?duel=)

The Duels realm's path: DUELS on the site, sign in or play as a guest, and the game goes straight into
the world, no character screen. With `?duel=1` (or `duel` in the page's env) the first roster is answered
with the account's duel body: the character last played, or, with a race and/or class asked for
(`?duel=orc-warrior`, `?duel=mage`, `?duel=gnome+warlock+f`), the highest-level one of those. With none,
one is made on the spot (a generated name, retried if taken; the realm starts it at 60 in the Lion's
Pride Inn) and entered. A full account enters the remembered character. Owner, 2026-10-21: "people hit
duels, sign in or are already logged in, enter waiting room, the inn with everyone, and then are placed
in a match in arena instantly".

